Subject: [PATCH v3 6/6] just: Notify after each process-email pass
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: otwkzmpmqsmtsvzutwtyonkpmnuvwrzv

just process-email runs unattended, so the operator learns what it did
only by reading the list. A notification per message lets them follow
the loop from a phone and know at once when it stops on a message it
could not answer.

The loop sends it, not the model, because only the loop knows from
the inbox whether the pass answered the message. A model asked to
notify may skip it, or report success for a pass that failed.

A failed or slow post must not stop the inbox from draining, so
notify gives up after ten seconds and only warns. Without a topic it
does nothing, so the loop still runs where no secret is set up.
